 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**No, the Aussie is strong against the yen right now. The yen is the weak currency.**\n\n- **Latest:** A$1 buys about **¥109.67** (October 2026, the most recent monthly reading).\n- **Past year:** up from about ¥100.84 in October 2025, so roughly 9% more yen per Aussie dollar.\n- **Recent peak:** ¥114.54 in August 2026. The Aussie has eased about 4% from that high.\n- **Longer view:** in early 2023 A$1 bought about ¥89–92. It has been above ¥100 since late 2024 and has been higher in 2026 than at any point in the period shown.\n\nSo a Japanese traveller or importer gets noticeably less value from the yen than a year ago, while an Australian buying Japanese goods or travel gets more.",
